            "repere": "Paragraphe · What is iron and what causes low iron?",
            "text": "What is iron and what causes low iron?",
            "image": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "settings": {
            "slot": "s953",
            "repere": "Paragraphe · Iron is an important mineral, helping …",
            "text": "Iron is an important mineral, helping deliver oxygen from our lungs to our entire body. Without adequate iron stores, you may not be able to get enough oxygen delivered to all your tissues, which could result in fatigue, muscle weakness upon exertion, pale skin and inability to stay warm.",
            "image": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "settings": {
            "slot": "s954",
            "repere": "Paragraphe · According to the CDC, 1 in 10 women is…",
            "text": "According to the CDC, 1 in 10 women is at risk for an iron deficiency.",
            "image": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "settings": {
            "slot": "s955",
            "repere": "Paragraphe · Low iron can be a result of low dietar…",
            "text": "Low iron can be a result of low dietary intake, poor absorption and/or excessive blood loss over time, increased demand during pregnancy.",
            "image": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
